  "verdict": "MARGINAL \u2014 IS significant but OOS fails (likely overfitting)",
  "conclusion": "Tested 4 sentiment/uncertainty indices (EPU, Michigan Sentiment, TED Spread, HY Spread) for incremental vol prediction beyond VIX. MARGINAL \u2014 IS significant but OOS fails (likely overfitting). This formally tests the NLP/sentiment channel and extends VIX sufficiency evidence to text-based uncertainty measures.",
  "implications": {
    "for_VT_strategy": "No sentiment overlay improves 12/VIX",
    "for_NLP_research": "Even sophisticated text-based indices (EPU from newspaper analysis) do not add value beyond VIX. The options market aggregates all publicly available sentiment information.",
    "next_steps": "Could test intraday Twitter/X sentiment (higher frequency than daily), or FinBERT on earnings call transcripts (firm-specific, not market-level). Market-level sentiment appears fully captured by VIX."
